[m
    docs(task-02): add backlog, sprint plan, Definition of Done and DevOps workflow[m
    [m
    Turn the frozen Task 1 scope into an executable plan.[m
    [m
    Stories and backlog[m
    - 24 user stories across 6 epics (access, master data, attendance capture,[m
      approval workflow, dashboard, delivery pipeline), each with testable[m
      Given/When/Then acceptance criteria rather than prose.[m
    - Acceptance criteria are traced back to the Task 1 success criteria (S1-S18),[m
      so every measurable target has a story that proves it.[m
    - Backlog prioritised with MoSCoW and estimated at 97 points, each story mapped[m
      to the task that delivers it.[m
    [m
    Process[m
    - Scrumban: 5 sprints over the 15 tasks, with a Kanban board whose columns have[m
      explicit entry rules and WIP limits, so an impediment stays visible instead of[m
      being worked around.[m
    - Definition of Ready (7 conditions) and Definition of Done (14 conditions[m
      spanning code, tests, pipeline and evidence), including an explicit "NOT Done"[m
      list that rules out skipped tests and unverified screenshots.[m
    [m
    Workflow[m
    - DevOps lifecycle diagram, Plan through Monitor, naming the tool at each stage[m
      and placing the quality gate between Test and Release. Authored as Mermaid so[m
      GitHub renders it natively, and rendered to PNG/SVG for the report.[m
    - Stage-to-tool mapping table and the feedback loop that Task 10 demonstrates[m
      concretely (inject defect, gate blocks deploy, fix, rerun to green).[m
    [m
    Tooling[m
    - scripts/capture/render-mermaid.js renders committed .mmd sources to PNG/SVG.[m
      Mermaid is declared in scripts/capture/package.json rather than vendored, as[m
      the bundle is ~3.5 MB; the renderer pins the SVG to its own viewBox because[m
      Mermaid emits width="100%", which otherwise collapses the diagram to the width[m
      of the surrounding caption.[m
    - .gitignore added, retaining docs/evidence/**/*.log so evidence logs stay[m
      committed alongside the screenshots rendered from them.[m
